      "message": "we added similar logic a while back because people manually unshallow dirs (see https://gerrit-review.git.corp.google.com/c/git-repo/+/558743). we should consolidate that logic into a new helper `_IsShallow` in project.py and use that rather than repeatedly checking .git/shallow and calling _SharingProjectHasShallow() across Sync_NetworkHalf, _RemoteFetch, and _CheckForImmutableRevision. then have a method like:\n```\ndef _ShouldVerifyUpstream(\n    self, use_superproject: Optional[bool] \u003d None, depth: Optional[int] \u003d None,\n) -\u003e bool:\n    \"\"\"Whether to verify upstream ancestry during immutable revision check.\"\"\"\n    if not (IsId(self.revisionExpr) and self.upstream):\n        return False\n    if self._UseSuperprojectForUpstream(use_superproject):\n        return True\n    return not self._IsShallow(depth)\n```\nthat gets overriden in MetaProjects to return false. that\u0027s simplify _CheckForImmutableRevision a good amount\n\nalso we should drop the `self.clone_depth` part and MetaProject check since MetaProject already overrides _SharingProjectHasShallow  to return False",
